        "original_id": "b23f407a-9e1c-58c8-a294-4fc63695f5dd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Walchelin de Ferriers, Richard I of England, Henry II of England, Eleanor of Aquitaine\n- Places: Oakham, Rutland\n- Buildings: Oakham Castle\n- Roles: Norman baron, principal captain, Lord of the Manor of Oakham\n\nFacts:\n- Richard I of England was the third of five sons of King Henry II of England and Duchess Eleanor of Aquitaine.\n- Oakham Castle in Oakham, Rutland, was constructed between 1180 and 1190 for Walchelin de Ferriers.\n- Walchelin de Ferriers was Lord of the Manor of Oakham.\n- Walchelin de Ferriers, also called Walkelin de Ferrers, was a Norman baron and a principal captain of King Richard I of England.\n- Walchelin de Ferriers died in 1201.",
